#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""xs: the only writer of the ledger. The ledger is the branch xs-ledger, checked out once at .xs/ledger:
the tracker (tasks, memory entries, the Log of each spec, ideas) and EVENTS.log. main holds the product and its
decisions; no command of xs commits to main. The state of every entry derives from its events (PROTOCOL P2, §3).

  xs install [--skills-dir DIR]            link the skills into each agent tool found in ~, or into DIR, with the tool's adapter
  xs init                                  in a repo: add AGENTS.md and project/ (and the adapters' files), keeping every file already there; create the ledger
  xs migrate                               once, in a repo that kept its tasks and EVENTS.log on main: move them to the ledger
  xs status [T12|S03|ADR-0007|L02] | --unlanded   the state of every entry, of one, or of the tasks closed and not yet on main
  xs status --since 2026-11-23             the report: every event since then
  xs agent T12|--branch b started|stopped|finished run=<id> ...   an agent's life (tool, model, effort, role, session;
                                           reason, resume_at, job; outcome); sent as an OpenTelemetry span when
                                           OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT is set
  xs handoff T12 --next "step" [--open "request"]...   package a started task for another session, account or tool
  xs takeover T12                          in any tool: prepare the worktree, apply the handed-off patch, print the brief
  xs sync                                  with a forge's merge train: record as landed the closed tasks it merged
  xs file [--type task|bug|prototype] [--priority p0|p1|p2|p3] [--spec S03] [--source TEXT] "title"
  xs ask  [--priority p0|p1|p2|p3] [--spec S03] "question"   a decision task for the owner
  xs next                                  tasks ready to start, p1 first; the WIP in use
  xs start T12 --branch t12-slug           claim T12 and create its worktree from main
  xs start T12 --branch b --run implementer   also launch AGENTS.md's "Agent implementer:" command there
  xs close T12                             the worker closes T12 once its Done section holds the proof: closed, then done when it lands
  xs answer T12                            the owner's answer is in T12's Done section: close it
  xs answer T12 "answer"                   write the owner's answer in T12's Done section, then close it
  xs block T12 "reason" | xs unblock T12 | xs drop T12 "why"
  xs review T12                            the lead opens a review round of a doing task (PROTOCOL §6)
  xs reviewed T12 approve|changes [--must-fix N]   the lead records the round's verdict and its must-fix findings
  xs spec S12 opened|ready|done|dropped    a spec's status; ready runs the readiness gate, done checks its invariant tests on main
  xs spec S12 approved|deviated|noted "line"   a dated line in the spec's Log, logs/S12.md in the ledger, with its event
  xs adr 0007 proposed|accepted|retired ["line"]   an ADR's status, as an event; the ADR file is never edited
  xs adr 0007 built "yes (T12)" | xs adr 0007 amended "ADR 0009 (what changed)"
  xs release <name> [--commit <sha>] | xs rollback <name> "reason"   a release and its rollback, as events
  xs incident open <slug> "line" [--sev 1|2|3|4] | resolve <slug>   an incident, for flow's time to restore
  xs import-git [--dry-run]                once, for a repo with history: the events git can date
  xs void T12 task.closed 2026-11-20T10:02:10Z "reason"   cancel a wrong event with a later one
  xs where [...] | xs land [...]           run the scripts where and land beside xs (zsh has a builtin where)

Memory (PROTOCOL §3): what an agent learns goes where its kind belongs; the agent proposes, the owner promotes.
  xs idea [--source TEXT] "idea"           one dated line in IDEAS.md of the ledger
  xs propose --kind rule|design|knowledge --anchor PATH --evidence TEXT [--to FILE] [--scope S] [--replaces L3] "entry"
                                           --replaces: the amended text of a stale entry; promoting it retires L3
  xs recommend L3 holds|retire "why"       the curator's recommendation on a stale entry, shown by xs queue
  xs promote L3                            the owner accepts: the entry is written in its destination, marked (L3);
                                           on a stale entry, the owner confirms it still holds
  xs checked L3 "check"                    a check enforces it: the entry leaves its destination
  xs retire L3 "why"                       the owner removes it
  xs repeated L3 "what was corrected"     a correction the entry should have prevented (curator)
  xs queue                                 what waits for the owner: open questions and proposals
  xs stale MAIN                            entries whose anchor this branch changed become stale
  xs load                                  for a session-start hook: records the recall of every loaded entry
  xs search "words"                        entries matching the words, best first; records each recall
Recalls go to the person's local log ($XS_HOME/events.log, default ~/.xs), never to git: one line per read.
XS_SESSION names the session in a recall.

An event line: <at> <scope> <subject> <kind> key=value ... (the contract of the ledger of events).
Each command is one commit of the ledger, under a lock. Agents may edit the text of a task or an entry in
.xs/ledger; xs commits that file with the next event about it, and refuses an EVENTS.log edited by hand.
In a team, when main has an upstream, xs pulls the ledger before each command and pushes it after; a rejected push
undoes the commit, pulls and runs the command again. XS_NO_PUSH=1 keeps the ledger local.
XS_LEDGER renames the branch (default xs-ledger); the ledger's commits are not signed unless XS_LEDGER_SIGN=1; XS_SCOPE overrides the scope (project/<repo folder>); XS_BY names
the actor (default: git user.name); MAIN names the base branch (default: main). The WIP limit is a line
"WIP limit: <n>" in AGENTS.md. start --run <agent> launches the line "Agent <agent>: <command>" of AGENTS.md in the
worktree, with the brief (--brief <file>, default the task file) as input; the log is in the git dir, xs-runs/<branch>.log.
A task with `after: T41` (or several, comma-separated) is not ready until each is done or dropped, or is doing or closed
on the branch it starts on: the chain it continues.
"""
import datetime as dt, fcntl, glob, json, os, re, shutil, subprocess, sys

LEDGER = os.environ.get("XS_LEDGER", "xs-ledger")
LOG = "EVENTS.log"
PRIO = {"p0": 0, "p1": 1, "p2": 2, "p3": 3}  # p0: an incident; it stops the line
TYPES = ("task", "bug", "decision", "prototype")
ATTRS = "EVENTS.log merge=union\nIDEAS.md merge=union\nlogs/*.md merge=union\n"
HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
# the tool's bookkeeping, one commit per command: unsigned, or every command would wait for a signing prompt
SIGN = [] if os.environ.get("XS_LEDGER_SIGN") else ["-c", "commit.gpgsign=false"]


def die(msg):
    sys.exit(f"xs: {msg}")


def git(*a, check=True, input=None):
    r = subprocess.run(["git", *a], capture_output=True, text=True, input=input)
    if check and r.returncode:
        die(f"git {' '.join(a)}: {r.stderr.strip()}")
    return r.stdout.strip()


def now():
    return dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def utc(iso):
    return dt.datetime.fromisoformat(iso).astimezone(dt.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def common():
    return git("rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir")


def main_wt():
    return re.match(r"worktree (.+)", git("worktree", "list", "--porcelain")).group(1)


def scope():
    if os.environ.get("XS_SCOPE"):
        return os.environ["XS_SCOPE"]
    return "project/" + os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(common()))


def actor():
    return re.sub(r"\s+", "_", os.environ.get("XS_BY") or git("config", "user.name", check=False) or "unknown")


def words(text):
    """Free text inside an event field: one token."""
    return re.sub(r"\s+", "_", text.strip())


# --- the ledger: a branch with no history in common with main, checked out once -------------------------------

_ledger = None


def remote_of_main():
    main = os.environ.get("MAIN", "main")
    if not git("rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", f"{main}@{{upstream}}", check=False):
        return None
    return git("config", f"branch.{main}.remote")


def upstream():
    """The remote the ledger follows: main's, in a team. None when solo or with XS_NO_PUSH."""
    return None if os.environ.get("XS_NO_PUSH") else remote_of_main()


def ledger():
    """The ledger's checkout, created on first use: from the remote's branch in a team, else as an orphan."""
    global _ledger
    if _ledger:
        return _ledger
    path = os.path.join(main_wt(), ".xs", "ledger")
    with Lock("xs-ledger-init.lock"):  # two first commands at once create it once
        if not os.path.isdir(path):
            create_ledger(path)
    _ledger = path
    return path


def create_ledger(path):
    exclude = os.path.join(common(), "info", "exclude")  # local: the ledger needs no commit on main
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(exclude), exist_ok=True)
    have = open(exclude).read() if os.path.exists(exclude) else ""
    if "/.xs/" not in have.split():
        open(exclude, "a").write(("" if have.endswith("\n") or not have else "\n") + "/.xs/\n")
    if not git("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"refs/heads/{LEDGER}", check=False):
        # Even with XS_NO_PUSH: a clone that started its own ledger would number tasks a teammate already holds.
        remote = remote_of_main()
        if remote and subprocess.run(["git", "fetch", "-q", remote, LEDGER], capture_output=True).returncode == 0:
            git("branch", LEDGER, "FETCH_HEAD")
        elif remote and git("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"refs/remotes/{remote}/{LEDGER}", check=False):
            git("branch", LEDGER, f"refs/remotes/{remote}/{LEDGER}")
        else:
            tree = git("mktree", input="")
            git("branch", LEDGER, git(*SIGN, "commit-tree", tree, "-m", "xs: the ledger"))
    git("worktree", "prune")  # a checkout deleted by hand still holds the branch until pruned
    git("worktree", "add", "-q", path, LEDGER)
    seeded = []
    tpl = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(HERE), "template", "ledger")
    for d, _, names in os.walk(tpl):
        for n in names:
            dst = os.path.join(path, os.path.relpath(os.path.join(d, n), tpl))
            if n != ".DS_Store" and not os.path.exists(dst):
                os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
                shutil.copy(os.path.join(d, n), dst)
                seeded.append(dst)
    for name, text in ((".gitattributes", ATTRS), (LOG, "")):
        if not os.path.exists(os.path.join(path, name)):
            open(os.path.join(path, name), "w").write(text)
            seeded.append(name)
    if seeded:
        git("-C", path, "add", "-A")
        git("-C", path, *SIGN, "commit", "-q", "--no-verify", "-m", "xs: seed the ledger")


def lpath(*parts):
    return os.path.join(ledger(), *parts)


class Lock:
    def __init__(self, name="xs-ledger.lock"):
        self.name = name

    def __enter__(self):
        self.f = open(os.path.join(common(), self.name), "w")
        fcntl.flock(self.f, fcntl.LOCK_EX)

    def __exit__(self, *_):
        self.f.close()


def unrecorded():
    """Events the integrator could not write after main had moved: the next command writes them first."""
    return os.path.join(common(), "xs-unrecorded.log")


def dirty(L):
    """The ledger's files with uncommitted text (a task's Done section, an answer): kept across an undone commit."""
    out = {}
    st = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", L, "status", "--porcelain", "-z", "-uall"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout
    for entry in st.split("\0"):  # not git(): its strip would eat the first entry's leading space
        p = os.path.join(L, entry[3:])
        if len(entry) > 3 and os.path.isfile(p):
            out[p] = open(p, "rb").read()
    return out


def txn(prepare):
    """One command, one commit of the ledger. prepare() validates against the ledger as it is now, edits files in it
    (never on main: a retry runs it again) and returns (event lines, paths relative to the ledger, commit message,
    result). In a team it runs after a pull, and again if a teammate's push came first: a claim taken meanwhile is
    refused by prepare itself."""
    global _state
    L, remote = ledger(), upstream()
    with Lock():
        for _ in range(3):
            if remote:
                r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", L, *SIGN, "pull", "-q", "--rebase", "--autostash", "--no-verify", remote, LEDGER],
                                   capture_output=True, text=True)
                if r.returncode and "couldn't find remote ref" not in r.stderr:
                    subprocess.run(["git", "-C", L, "rebase", "--abort"], capture_output=True)  # never leave it mid-rebase
                    die(f"pull of the ledger from {remote} failed: {r.stderr.strip()}")
            log = os.path.join(L, LOG)
            if (open(log).read() if os.path.exists(log) else "").strip() != git("-C", L, "show", f"HEAD:{LOG}", check=False):
                die(f"{log} has changes xs did not make: the log only grows through xs. Undo them: git -C {L} checkout {LOG}")
            _state = None
            kept = dirty(L)
            have = set(open(log).readlines()) if os.path.exists(log) else set()
            pending = [l for l in (open(unrecorded()).readlines() if os.path.exists(unrecorded()) else []) if l not in have]
            lines, paths, msg, result = prepare()
            lines = pending + lines
            if lines:
                with open(log, "a") as f:
                    f.writelines(lines)
            paths = sorted(set(paths) | ({LOG} if lines else set()))
            if paths:
                git("-C", L, "add", "-A", "--", *paths)
            if not paths or not git("-C", L, "diff", "--cached", "--name-only"):
                return result
            git("-C", L, *SIGN, "commit", "-q", "--no-verify", "-m", msg, "--", *paths)
            _state = None
            r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", L, "push", "-q", "--no-verify", remote, f"{LEDGER}:{LEDGER}"],
                               capture_output=True, text=True) if remote else None
            rejected = r and r.returncode and ("rejected" in r.stderr or "fetch first" in r.stderr)
            if not rejected:
                if pending:
                    os.remove(unrecorded())  # the local commit holds them now
                if r and r.returncode:
                    die(f"push of the ledger to {remote} failed: {r.stderr.strip()}")
                return result
            # A teammate pushed first: undo the commit, put back the text that was there before, pull, decide again.
            git("-C", L, "reset", "-q", "--hard", "HEAD~1")
            for p, data in kept.items():
                os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)
                open(p, "wb").write(data)
        die(f"the ledger on {remote} kept moving: run the command again")


def ev(subject, kind, at=None, **kv):
    fields = " ".join(f"{k}={v}" for k, v in kv.items() if v not in (None, ""))
    return f"{at or now()} {scope()} {subject} {kind} {fields}".rstrip() + "\n"


def rel(path):
    return os.path.relpath(path, ledger())


# --- state, derived from the events ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

_state = None
LINE = re.compile(r"^(\S+) (\S+) (\S+) (\S+)(.*)$")


def events(text=None):
    if text is None:
        log = lpath(LOG)
        text = open(log).read() if os.path.exists(log) else ""
    out = []
    for line in text.splitlines():
        m = LINE.match(line)
        if m:
            at, sc, subj, kind, rest = m.groups()
            out.append(dict(at=at, subj=subj, kind=kind, kv=dict(re.findall(r"(\w+)=(\S+)", rest)), line=line))
    void = {(e["subj"], e["kv"].get("of_kind"), e["kv"].get("of_at")) for e in out if e["kind"] == "event.voided"}
    return [e for e in out if e["kind"] != "event.voided" and (e["subj"], e["kind"], e["at"]) not in void]


def state_of(evs):
    out = {}
    for e in evs:
        d = out.setdefault(e["subj"], {})
        if e["kind"].startswith("agent."):  # an agent's life: beside the task's state, never its last event
            d.setdefault("agents", {})[e["kv"].get("run", "-")] = e
            continue
        d["last"] = e
        for k in ("status", "branch", "built", "amended"):
            if e["kv"].get(k):
                d[k] = e["kv"][k]
    return out


def state():
    """subject -> its status, its branch, and its last event."""
    global _state
    if _state is None:
        _state = state_of(events())
    return _state


def status_of(subject, default=""):
    return state().get(subject, {}).get("status", default)


def spec_status(sid):
    return "ready" if sid == "S00" else status_of(sid, "draft")  # S00 holds the product's invariants and never closes


# --- files -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def find(tid):
    hits = glob.glob(lpath("tasks", f"{tid}-*.md"))
    if len(hits) != 1:
        die(f"{tid}: {'no task file' if not hits else 'several task files'} in {lpath('tasks')}")
    return hits[0]


def front(path):
    text = open(path).read()
    m = re.match(r"---\n(.*?\n)---\n", text, re.S)
    if not m:
        die(f"{path} has no frontmatter")
    return text, m


def get(path, key):
    _, m = front(path)
    v = re.search(rf"^{key}:[ \t]*([^\s#]*)", m.group(1), re.M)
    return v.group(1) if v else ""


def get_line(path, key):
    _, m = front(path)
    v = re.search(rf"^{key}:[ \t]*(.*)$", m.group(1), re.M)
    return v.group(1) if v else ""


def ident(path):
    return os.path.basename(path).split("-")[0]


def next_id(folder, prefix):
    nums = [int(m.group(1)) for p in glob.glob(lpath(folder, f"{prefix}*-*.md")) if (m := re.match(rf"{prefix}(\d+)-", os.path.basename(p)))]
    return f"{prefix}{max(nums, default=0) + 1:02d}"


def check_text(path):
    """A task's text: its type and priority inside the vocabulary, and no state, which lives in the events."""
    if get(path, "status"):
        die(f"{path} has a status: line: state lives in the ledger's events, remove the line")
    if get(path, "type") not in TYPES:
        die(f"{path} has type: {get(path, 'type') or 'nothing'}, outside {'|'.join(TYPES)}")
    if get(path, "priority") not in PRIO:
        die(f"{path} has priority: {get(path, 'priority') or 'nothing'}, outside p0|p1|p2|p3")


def need_done(path):
    if not re.search(r"^## Done[ \t]*$", open(path).read(), re.M):
        die(f"{path} has no Done section: add the command that proves it, then close")


def opt(args, name, default=""):
    if name in args:
        i = args.index(name)
        if i + 1 >= len(args):
            die(f"{name} needs a value")
        v = args[i + 1]
        del args[i:i + 2]
        return v
    return default


def tasks():
    return sorted(glob.glob(lpath("tasks", "T*-*.md")), key=lambda p: int(re.match(r"T(\d+)-", os.path.basename(p)).group(1)))


# --- tasks -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def file_task(args, kind):
    typ = "decision" if kind == "question.asked" else opt(args, "--type", "task")
    prio, spec, source = opt(args, "--priority", "p2"), opt(args, "--spec"), opt(args, "--source")
    if typ not in TYPES or prio not in PRIO or len(args) != 1:
        die('usage: xs file [--type task|bug|prototype] [--priority p0|p1|p2|p3] [--spec S03] [--source TEXT] "title"')
    title = args[0]
    slug = "-".join(re.findall(r"[a-z0-9]+", title.lower())[:6]) or "task"
    fm = [f"title: {title}", f"type: {typ}", f"priority: {prio}", f"created: {dt.date.today().isoformat()}"] + \
        [f"{k}: {v}" for k, v in (("source", source), ("spec", spec)) if v]
    body = "## What\n\n## Why\n\n## Where\n\n## Done when\n" if typ != "decision" else "## Question\n\n## Options\n\n## Recommendation\n"

    def prepare():
        tid = next_id("tasks", "T")  # one ledger: the numbers never collide between branches
        path = lpath("tasks", f"{tid}-{slug}.md")
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
        open(path, "w").write("---\n" + "\n".join(fm) + "\n---\n\n" + body)
        line = ev(tid, kind, status="todo", type=typ, priority=prio, spec=spec.split()[0] if spec else "", by=actor())
        return [line], [rel(path)], f"xs: file {tid} {title}", (tid, path)
    tid, path = txn(prepare)
    print(f"{tid} {path}")


def ready(tid, path, branch=None):
    """Why the task cannot start, or ''."""
    status = status_of(tid)
    if status != "todo":
        return f"status is {status or 'missing'}"
    spec = re.search(r"\bS\d+\b", get_line(path, "spec"))
    if spec and spec_status(spec.group(0)) != "ready":
        return f"its spec {spec.group(0)} is not ready"
    return after_open(path, branch)


def after_open(path, branch=None):
    """The first task named in `after:` that is neither done nor dropped, as a reason, or ''.
    A task doing or closed on the branch being started is the previous link of the same chain: it does not block."""
    for t in re.findall(r"\bT\d+\b", get_line(path, "after")):
        st = state().get(t, {})
        status = st.get("status", "missing")
        if status not in ("done", "dropped") and not (branch and status in ("doing", "closed") and st.get("branch") == branch):
            return f"it comes after {t}, which is {status}"
    return ""


def wip():
    limit = re.search(r"WIP limit:\s*(\d+)", open("AGENTS.md").read(), re.I) if os.path.exists("AGENTS.md") else None
    return sum(status_of(ident(p)) == "doing" for p in tasks()), int(limit.group(1)) if limit else None


def cmd_next(args):
    rows = [(PRIO.get(get(p, "priority"), 9), p) for p in tasks() if not ready(ident(p), p)]
    for _, p in sorted(rows, key=lambda r: r[0]):
        print(f"{ident(p)} {get(p, 'priority')} {get(p, 'type')} {get_line(p, 'title')}")
    doing, limit = wip()
    print(f"doing: {doing}" + (f" of {limit}" if limit else " (no WIP limit)"))


def cmd_start(args):
    branch, run, brief = opt(args, "--branch"), opt(args, "--run"), opt(args, "--brief")
    if len(args) != 1 or not branch:
        die("usage: xs start T12 --branch <branch> [--run <agent> [--brief <file>]]")
    command = agent_command(run) if run else None
    tid, main = args[0], os.environ.get("MAIN", "main")
    path = find(tid)
    check_text(path)

    def prepare():  # after the pull, in a team: a claim pushed by a teammate is seen here
        st = state().get(tid, {})
        if st.get("status") == "doing":
            if st.get("branch") != branch:
                die(f"{tid} is doing on {st.get('branch')}: claimed elsewhere, run xs next")
            return [], [], "", None  # idempotent: run again, it only recreates a missing worktree
        why = ready(tid, path, branch)
        if why:
            die(f"{tid} cannot start: {why}")
        doing, limit = wip()
        if limit is not None and doing >= limit:
            die(f"WIP limit reached: {doing} of {limit} tasks doing (AGENTS.md)")
        line = ev(tid, "task.started", status="doing", branch=branch, by=actor(), agent=run or None)
        return [line], [rel(path)], f"xs: start {tid} on {branch}", None
    txn(prepare)
    wt = os.path.join(main_wt(), ".xs", "worktrees", branch)
    if not os.path.isdir(wt):  # idempotent: the claim may have been recorded before a crash
        exists = git("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"refs/heads/{branch}", check=False)
        git("worktree", "add", "-q", wt, *([branch] if exists else ["-b", branch, main]))
    print(f"{tid} doing on {branch}\nworktree: {wt}\ntask: {path}")
    if command:  # outside the claim: at least once, a second start launches it again
        brief = os.path.abspath(brief or path)
        logs = os.path.join(common(), "xs-runs")
        os.makedirs(logs, exist_ok=True)
        out = os.path.join(logs, f"{branch}.log")
        xs, q = os.path.join(HERE, "xs"), tid
        # the agent's life as events: started now, finished or stopped (reason=error) when the command exits; run = the shell's pid
        wrapped = (f"( {command} ); rc=$?; if [ $rc -eq 0 ]; then \"{xs}\" agent {q} finished run={run}-$$ exit=0; "
                   f"else \"{xs}\" agent {q} stopped run={run}-$$ reason=error exit=$rc; fi")
        with open(brief) as i, open(out, "a") as o:
            p = subprocess.Popen(wrapped, shell=True, cwd=wt, stdin=i, stdout=o, stderr=o, start_new_session=True)
        cmd_agent([tid, "started", f"run={run}-{p.pid}", f"role={run}"])
        print(f"agent: {run} (pid {p.pid}), log: {out}")


def agent_command(name):
    """The headless command AGENTS.md declares for an agent: a line "Agent <name>: <command>"."""
    text = open("AGENTS.md").read() if os.path.exists("AGENTS.md") else ""
    m = re.search(rf"^[-*\s]*Agent {re.escape(name)}:\s*`?([^`\n]+?)`?\s*$", text, re.M)
    if not m:
        die(f"no agent {name} in AGENTS.md: add a line \"Agent {name}: <headless command>\"")
    return m.group(1)


# --- agents (PROTOCOL §8): one agent's life as events, the same for every tool ------------------------------------

# reason: ACP's stopReason (end_turn, max_tokens, max_turn_requests, refusal, cancelled), and what ACP does not carry
STOPS = ("end_turn", "max_tokens", "max_turn_requests", "refusal", "cancelled", "limit", "error", "killed")
AGENT_KEYS = {"started": ("run", "tool", "model", "effort", "role", "session"),
              "stopped": ("run", "reason", "resume_at", "job", "exit"),
              "finished": ("run", "outcome", "exit")}


def cmd_agent(args):
    """xs agent T12|--branch b started|stopped|finished key=value ...: written by xs start --run, a tool's hook, or the lead."""
    branch = opt(args, "--branch")
    usage = "usage: xs agent T12|--branch <b> started|stopped|finished run=<id> [" + \
            "; ".join(f"{k}: {' '.join(v[1:])}" for k, v in AGENT_KEYS.items()) + "]"
    if branch:
        doing = [t for t, d in state().items() if re.match(r"T\d+$", t) and d.get("status") == "doing" and d.get("branch") == branch]
        if not doing:
            print(f"no task doing on {branch}: nothing recorded")
            return  # a hook in a session outside the factory: never an error
        args = [doing[0]] + args
    if len(args) < 2 or args[1] not in AGENT_KEYS:
        die(usage)
    tid, what = args[0], args[1]
    find(tid)
    if not state().get(tid, {}).get("branch"):
        print(f"{tid} was never started: nothing recorded")
        return  # a hook saw a task named in a prompt that no xs start claimed
    kv = dict(a.split("=", 1) for a in args[2:] if "=" in a)
    bad = [k for k in kv if k not in AGENT_KEYS[what]] + [a for a in args[2:] if "=" not in a]
    if bad or any(not re.fullmatch(r"[\w.:@/+-]+", v) for v in kv.values()):
        die(f"{' '.join(bad) or 'a value with a space or a quote'}: {usage}")
    if what == "stopped" and kv.get("reason") not in STOPS:
        die(f"reason is one of {', '.join(STOPS)}")
    if what == "finished" and not kv.get("outcome"):
        kv["outcome"] = status_of(tid, "todo")  # closed, blocked, or still doing: the agent ended without closing it
    kv.setdefault("run", "-")
    line = ev(tid, f"agent.{what}", **kv)
    txn(lambda: ([line], [], f"xs: agent {what} on {tid}", None))
    export([line])
    print(line.strip())


def export(lines):
    """With OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT set, an agent's run goes out as one OpenTelemetry span (GenAI conventions)
    when it ends: from agent.started to agent.stopped or agent.finished, one trace per task. Never fails a command."""
    url = os.environ.get("OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT") or \
        (os.environ["OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT"].rstrip("/") + "/v1/traces" if os.environ.get("OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT") else "")
    spans = [s for s in (span_of(e) for e in events("".join(lines))) if s]
    if not url or not spans:
        return
    import urllib.request
    headers = {"Content-Type": "application/json"}
    for h in filter(None, os.environ.get("OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS", "").split(",")):
        k, _, v = h.partition("=")
        headers[k.strip()] = urllib.request.unquote(v.strip())
    body = {"resourceSpans": [{"resource": {"attributes": attrs({"service.name": os.environ.get("OTEL_SERVICE_NAME", "xs"), "xs.scope": scope()})},
                               "scopeSpans": [{"scope": {"name": "xs"}, "spans": spans}]}]}
    try:
        urllib.request.urlopen(urllib.request.Request(url, json.dumps(body).encode(), headers), timeout=5)
    except Exception as e:  # the ledger holds the event: the exporter is a copy
        print(f"xs: OTLP export to {url} failed: {e}", file=sys.stderr)


def attrs(d):
    return [{"key": k, "value": {"stringValue": str(v)}} for k, v in d.items() if v not in (None, "", "-")]


def span_of(end):
    """The span of a run that ended with this event, or None."""
    import hashlib
    if end["kind"] not in ("agent.stopped", "agent.finished"):
        return None
    run, tid = end["kv"].get("run", "-"), end["subj"]
    start = next((e for e in reversed(events()) if e["subj"] == tid and e["kind"] == "agent.started"
                  and e["kv"].get("run", "-") == run and e["at"] <= end["at"]), None)
    s = (start or end)["kv"]
    ns = lambda at: str(int(dt.datetime.fromisoformat(at.replace("Z", "+00:00")).timestamp() * 1e9))
    h = lambda x, n: hashlib.sha256(x.encode()).hexdigest()[:n]
    reason = end["kv"].get("reason")
    return {"traceId": h(f"{scope()} {tid}", 32), "spanId": h(f"{scope()} {tid} {run} {(start or end)['at']}", 16),
            "name": f"invoke_agent {s.get('role') or tid}", "kind": 1,
            "startTimeUnixNano": ns((start or end)["at"]), "endTimeUnixNano": ns(end["at"]),
            "attributes": attrs({"gen_ai.operation.name": "invoke_agent", "gen_ai.agent.name": s.get("role"),
                                 "gen_ai.provider.name": s.get("tool"), "gen_ai.request.model": s.get("model"),
                                 "gen_ai.conversation.id": s.get("session"), "xs.task": tid, "xs.run": run,
                                 "xs.effort": s.get("effort"), "xs.reason": reason, "xs.outcome": end["kv"].get("outcome"),
                                 "xs.resume_at": end["kv"].get("resume_at"), "xs.job": end["kv"].get("job")}),
            "status": {"code": 2 if reason in ("error", "killed", "refusal") else 1}}


# --- handoff (PROTOCOL §8): the state of a task in git, so that any tool can take it over -------------------------

def worktree_of(branch):
    return os.path.join(main_wt(), ".xs", "worktrees", branch)


def cmd_handoff(args):
    """Package a task for another session, account or tool: a brief, the branch's head, the uncommitted work as a patch."""
    nxt, opened = opt(args, "--next"), []
    while "--open" in args:
        opened.append(opt(args, "--open"))
    if len(args) != 1 or not nxt:
        die('usage: xs handoff T12 --next "the next step" [--open "a request of the owner not yet done"]...')
    tid = args[0]
    path, d = find(tid), state().get(tid, {})
    branch = d.get("branch")
    if not branch or d.get("status") not in ("doing", "blocked", "closed"):
        die(f"{tid} is {d.get('status', 'todo')}: only a started task is handed off; a new one starts with xs start")
    wt, stamp = worktree_of(branch), now().replace(":", "")
    head = git("rev-parse", "--short", branch, check=False) or "none"
    patch = ""
    if os.path.isdir(wt):  # the uncommitted work, untracked files included, without touching the worktree's index
        idx = os.path.join(common(), f"xs-handoff-{os.getpid()}.index")
        env = {**os.environ, "GIT_INDEX_FILE": idx}
        subprocess.run(["git", "-C", wt, "read-tree", "HEAD"], env=env, check=True)
        subprocess.run(["git", "-C", wt, "add", "-A"], env=env, check=True)
        patch = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", wt, "diff", "--cached", "--binary", "HEAD"], env=env, capture_output=True, text=True).stdout
        os.remove(idx)
    agent = next((e for e in reversed(events()) if e["subj"] == tid and e["kind"] == "agent.started"), None)
    a = agent["kv"] if agent else {}
    name = f"{tid}-{stamp}"
    body = f"""# Handoff of {tid}: {get_line(path, 'title')}

Handed off on {now()} by {actor()}.

- Task: {rel(path)} ({d.get('status')}), spec: {get(path, 'spec') or 'none'}
- Branch: {branch} at {head}; worktree: .xs/worktrees/{branch}
- Uncommitted work: {f'handoffs/{name}.patch ({len(patch.splitlines())} lines), applied by xs takeover' if patch else 'none'}
- Last agent: {' '.join(f'{k}={v}' for k, v in a.items()) if a else 'none recorded'}

## Next step

{nxt}

## Open requests of the owner

{chr(10).join(f'- {o}' for o in opened) or '- none'}

## Brief

You take over {tid} from another session. Run `xs takeover {tid}` from the repo: it prepares the worktree
.xs/worktrees/{branch} with the work left uncommitted, and prints this file. Then read the task file, `xs status {tid}`
and the Log of its spec before anything else; do not rebuild the state from a chat. Do the next step above, then
each open request, filing with `xs file` what you do not do.
""" + (f"The same tool can resume the session itself instead: session {a['session']} (ACP `session/load`).\n" if a.get("session") else "")

    def prepare():
        os.makedirs(lpath("handoffs"), exist_ok=True)
        open(lpath("handoffs", name + ".md"), "w").write(body)
        files = [f"handoffs/{name}.md"]
        if patch:
            open(lpath("handoffs", name + ".patch"), "w").write(patch)
            files.append(f"handoffs/{name}.patch")
        return [ev(tid, "task.handed_off", file=f"handoffs/{name}.md", head=head, by=actor())], files, f"xs: hand off {tid}", None
    txn(prepare)
    remote = upstream()
    if remote and not os.environ.get("XS_NO_PUSH") and head != "none":  # another machine takes it over from the remote
        git("push", "-q", remote, f"{branch}:{branch}", check=False)
    print(f"handed off {tid}: {lpath('handoffs', name + '.md')}")


def cmd_takeover(args):
    """Take over a handed-off task, in any tool: prepare its worktree, apply its patch, print its brief."""
    if len(args) != 1:
        die("usage: xs takeover T12")
    tid = args[0]
    find(tid)
    last = next((e for e in reversed(events()) if e["subj"] == tid and e["kind"] == "task.handed_off"), None)
    if not last:
        die(f"{tid} has no handoff: take a stopped session over by the lead's rule (its last prompts, xs file what is open)")
    md = lpath(last["kv"]["file"])
    branch, head = state()[tid]["branch"], last["kv"].get("head")
    wt = worktree_of(branch)
    if not git("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"refs/heads/{branch}", check=False) and upstream():
        git("fetch", "-q", upstream(), f"{branch}:{branch}", check=False)
    if not os.path.isdir(wt):
        if not git("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"refs/heads/{branch}", check=False):
            die(f"no branch {branch} here or on the remote: the handoff names a head that never left its machine")
        git("worktree", "add", "-q", wt, branch)
    now_head = git("-C", wt, "rev-parse", "--short", "HEAD")
    if head not in (None, "none") and now_head != head:
        print(f"note: {branch} is at {now_head}, the handoff was at {head}: read what changed since")
    patch = md[:-3] + ".patch"
    if os.path.exists(patch):
        if subprocess.run(["git", "-C", wt, "apply", "--check", patch], capture_output=True).returncode == 0:
            git("-C", wt, "apply", patch)
            print(f"applied {patch}")
        elif subprocess.run(["git", "-C", wt, "apply", "--reverse", "--check", patch], capture_output=True).returncode == 0:
            print("the uncommitted work is already in the worktree")
        else:
            die(f"{patch} does not apply to {wt}: it has other changes; resolve them, then run xs takeover again")
    txn(lambda: ([ev(tid, "task.taken_over", file=last["kv"]["file"], by=actor())], [], f"xs: take over {tid}", None))
    print(f"worktree: {wt}\n")
    print(open(md).read().rstrip())


def forge_of():
    f = os.environ.get("LAND_FORGE")
    if f is None and os.path.isfile("AGENTS.md"):
        m = re.search(r"^- Merge train:\s*(github|gitlab)\b", open("AGENTS.md").read(), re.M)
        f = m and m.group(1)
    return f or None


def forge_rejects(forge, branch):
    """Why the forge holds the branch's request back (red, changes-requested, conflict, closed), or None."""
    cmd = ["gh", "pr", "view", branch, "--json", "state,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,statusCheckRollup"] if forge == "github" \
        else ["glab", "mr", "view", branch, "-F", "json"]
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
        r = json.loads(p.stdout) if p.returncode == 0 else None
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        r = None
    if not isinstance(r, dict):
        return None  # no request, or no CLI: nothing to say
    if forge == "github":
        bad = {"FAILURE", "ERROR", "CANCELLED", "TIMED_OUT", "ACTION_REQUIRED"}
        checks = r.get("statusCheckRollup") or []
        return ("closed" if r.get("state") == "CLOSED" else
                "red" if any((c.get("conclusion") or c.get("state")) in bad for c in checks) else
                "changes-requested" if r.get("reviewDecision") == "CHANGES_REQUESTED" else
                "conflict" if r.get("mergeStateStatus") == "DIRTY" else None)
    pipe = r.get("head_pipeline") or r.get("pipeline") or {}
    return ("closed" if r.get("state") == "closed" else
            "red" if pipe.get("status") in ("failed", "canceled") else
            "changes-requested" if r.get("detailed_merge_status") == "requested_changes" else
            "conflict" if r.get("has_conflicts") else None)


def cmd_sync(args):
    """With a forge (Merge train: github|gitlab), the forge moves main: record the tasks whose branch it merged,
    and as ejected those whose request it holds back (a red pipeline, changes requested, a conflict, closed)."""
    main = os.environ.get("MAIN", "main")
    remote = remote_of_main() or "origin"
    git("fetch", "-q", remote, main)
    on = f"{remote}/{main}"
    forge = forge_of()
    if forge and not shutil.which("gh" if forge == "github" else "glab"):
        print(f"xs: {'gh' if forge == 'github' else 'glab'} not found: ejections not checked", file=sys.stderr)

    def prepare():
        merged, ejected = {}, {}
        for t, d in state().items():
            b = d.get("branch")
            if not (re.match(r"T\d+$", t) and d.get("status") == "closed" and b and git("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"refs/heads/{b}", check=False)):
                continue
            if not any(l.startswith("+") for l in git("cherry", on, b).splitlines()):  # by patch: a rebase merge counts
                merged[t] = b
            elif forge:
                why = forge_rejects(forge, b)
                last = d.get("last") or {}
                if why and not (last.get("kind") == "land.ejected" and last["kv"].get("reason") == why):  # once per reason
                    ejected[t] = (b, why)
        head = git("rev-parse", "--short", on)
        lines = [ev(t, "landed", status="done", on=main, commit=head, branch=b, by="forge") for t, b in sorted(merged.items())]
        lines += [ev(t, "land.ejected", branch=b, reason=why, by="forge") for t, (b, why) in sorted(ejected.items())]
        return lines, [], "xs: sync from the forge", (merged, ejected)
    merged, ejected = txn(prepare)
    for t, b in sorted(merged.items()):
        print(f"{t} landed by the forge ({b})")
    for t, (b, why) in sorted(ejected.items()):
        print(f"{t} ejected by the forge ({b}): {why}")
    if not merged and not ejected:
        print(f"nothing new on {on}")


def nothing_to_land(branch):
    """No branch, or a branch whose every change is on main (cherry-picked by the integrator counts)."""
    if not branch:
        return True
    if not git("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"refs/heads/{branch}", check=False):
        return False  # gone: cannot tell, the integrator's landed event decides
    return not any(l.startswith("+") for l in git("cherry", os.environ.get("MAIN", "main"), branch).splitlines())


def transition(args, kind, status, need_reason=False):
    if len(args) != (2 if need_reason else 1):
        die(f"usage: xs {sys.argv[1]} T12" + (' "reason"' if need_reason else ""))
    tid = args[0]
    path = find(tid)

    def prepare():
        current, new = status_of(tid), status
        if current in ("done", "dropped") or (current == "closed" and kind != "task.dropped"):
            die(f"{tid} is already {current}")
        if kind in ("task.closed", "question.answered"):
            check_text(path)
            need_done(path)
        if kind == "question.answered" and get(path, "type") != "decision":
            die(f"{tid} is not a decision task: close it with xs close")
        if kind == "task.closed" and get(path, "type") == "decision":
            die(f"{tid} is a decision: close it with xs answer")
        if kind == "task.unblocked":
            if current != "blocked":
                die(f"{tid} is not blocked")
            new = "doing" if state().get(tid, {}).get("branch") else "todo"
        if kind == "task.closed" and nothing_to_land(state().get(tid, {}).get("branch")):
            new = "done"  # never started, or its branch is already on main: no integrator would ever land it
        if need_reason:
            with open(path, "a") as f:
                f.write(f"\n{'Dropped' if kind == 'task.dropped' else 'Blocked'}: {args[1]}\n")
        line = ev(tid, kind, status=new, reason=words(args[1]) if need_reason else None, by=actor())
        files = [rel(f) for f in glob.glob(lpath("tasks", f"{tid}-*"))]  # the task and its saved patch, if any
        return [line], files, f"xs: {kind.split('.')[1]} {tid}", new
    new = txn(prepare)
    print(f"{tid} {new}" + (": it is done once the integrator lands its branch" if new == "closed" else ""))


def cmd_answer(args):
    """xs answer T12 ["answer"]: with the answer, write it in the task's Done section first."""
    if len(args) == 2:
        path = find(args[0])
        if get(path, "type") != "decision":
            die(f"{args[0]} is not a decision task: close it with xs close")
        if status_of(args[0]) in ("done", "dropped"):
            die(f"{args[0]} is already {status_of(args[0])}")
        if not args[1].strip() or "\n" in args[1]:
            die("the answer is one line, not empty")
        text = open(path).read().rstrip("\n")
        m = re.search(r"^## Done[ \t]*$", text, re.M)
        if not m:
            text += f"\n\n## Done\n\n{args[1]}"
        else:
            # At the end of the Done section: before the next heading, or at the file's end.
            nxt = re.search(r"^## ", text[m.end():], re.M)
            at = m.end() + nxt.start() if nxt else len(text)
            text = text[:at].rstrip("\n") + f"\n\n{args[1]}" + ("\n\n" + text[at:] if nxt else "")
        with open(path, "w") as f:
            f.write(text + "\n")
        args = args[:1]
    transition(args, "question.answered", "done")


# --- specs and ADRs: their text on main, their state in the ledger -----------------------------------------------

def spec_file(sid):
    hits = glob.glob(f"project/specs/{sid}-*.md")
    if len(hits) != 1:
        die(f"{sid}: no single spec file in project/specs")
    return hits[0]


def test_names(path):
    return re.findall(r"Test: `([^`]+)`", open(path).read())


def missing_tests(path, main):
    """The invariant tests the spec names that main does not hold, outside project/: in any case, spaces or underscores."""
    out = []
    for name in test_names(path):
        rx = re.sub(r"\\?[ _]", "[ _]", re.escape(name))
        if subprocess.run(["git", "grep", "-qiE", "-e", rx, main, "--", ".", ":!project"], capture_output=True).returncode:
            out.append(name)
    return out


def open_round(tid, evs):
    """The round of the task's open review: its last review.started, if no verdict of that round follows it."""
    starts = [i for i, e in enumerate(evs) if e["kind"] == "review.started"]
    if not starts:
        return None
    rnd = evs[starts[-1]]["kv"].get("round")
    return None if any(e["kind"] == "review.verdict" and e["kv"].get("round") == rnd for e in evs[starts[-1] + 1:]) else rnd


def cmd_review(args):
    """The lead opens a review round of a doing task; the tool counts the rounds, so that
    "stop after three review rounds" reads from the ledger."""
    if len(args) != 1:
        die("usage: xs review T12")
    tid = args[0]
    find(tid)

    def prepare():
        if status_of(tid) != "doing":
            die(f"{tid} is {status_of(tid) or 'without a status'}: only a doing task is reviewed")
        rnd = 1 + sum(e["kind"] == "review.started" for e in events() if e["subj"] == tid)
        return [ev(tid, "review.started", round=rnd, by=actor())], [], f"xs: review {tid} round {rnd}", rnd
    print(f"{tid} review round {txn(prepare)}")


def cmd_reviewed(args):
    """The verdict of the open review round, with the number of its must-fix findings."""
    must = opt(args, "--must-fix", "0")
    if len(args) != 2 or args[1] not in ("approve", "changes"):
        die("usage: xs reviewed T12 approve|changes [--must-fix N]")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"\d+", must):
        die(f"--must-fix takes a whole number, not {must}")
    tid, verdict, must = args[0], args[1], int(must)
    if verdict == "approve" and must:
        die(f"{tid}: an approval leaves no must-fix open; record {must} must-fix with changes")
    find(tid)

    def prepare():
        rnd = open_round(tid, [e for e in events() if e["subj"] == tid])
        if not rnd:
            die(f"{tid} has no open review: open one with xs review {tid}")
        return [ev(tid, "review.verdict", verdict=verdict, round=rnd, must_fix=must, by=actor())], [], f"xs: reviewed {tid} round {rnd}", rnd
    rnd = txn(prepare)
    print(f"{tid} review round {rnd} {verdict}")
    if verdict == "changes" and int(rnd) >= 3:
        print(f"xs: warning: round {rnd} asks for changes; PROTOCOL §6 says stop after three review rounds "
              "and return to Definition", file=sys.stderr)


def cmd_spec(args):
    kinds = {"opened": "draft", "ready": "ready", "done": "done", "dropped": "dropped", "approved": "", "deviated": "", "noted": ""}
    lined = ("approved", "deviated", "noted")
    if len(args) < 2 or args[1] not in kinds or (args[1] in lined) != (len(args) == 3):
        die('usage: xs spec S12 opened|ready|done|dropped, or xs spec S12 approved|deviated|noted "line"')
    sid, kind = args[0], args[1]
    if sid == "S00" and kind in ("done", "dropped"):
        die("S00 never closes: it holds the invariants of the whole product")
    path = spec_file(sid)
    if kind == "ready":
        fails = readiness(sid, path)
        if fails:
            die(f"{sid} is not ready:\n" + "\n".join(f"  {i}. {f}" for i, f in enumerate(fails, 1)))
    if kind == "done":
        main = os.environ.get("MAIN", "main")
        gone = missing_tests(path, main)
        if gone:
            die(f"{sid} names tests that {main} does not hold: " + "; ".join(gone) + ". Land them before closing the spec")

    def prepare():
        paths = []
        if kind in lined:  # the Log only grows, one dated line each
            log = lpath("logs", f"{sid}.md")
            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(log), exist_ok=True)
            who = {"approved": f"approved by {actor()}: ", "deviated": "deviated: ", "noted": ""}[kind]
            with open(log, "a") as f:
                f.write(f"- {dt.date.today().isoformat()}: {who}{args[2]}\n")
            paths.append(rel(log))
        line = ev(sid, f"spec.{'closed' if kind == 'done' else kind}", status=kinds[kind], by=actor())
        return [line], paths, f"xs: spec {sid} {kind}", None
    txn(prepare)
    print(f"{sid} {kind}" + (f": {spec_status(sid)}" if kinds[kind] else f", in {lpath('logs', sid + '.md')}"))


def readiness(sid, path):
    """The readiness gate of PROTOCOL §4, as far as text and events can show it: every failure, not only the first.
    Whether the outcome is verifiable by someone else stays the reviewer's judgment; this catches what is missing."""
    text = open(path).read()
    sec = {m.group(1).strip(): m.group(2) for m in re.finditer(r"^## (.+)\n((?:(?!^## ).*\n?)*)", text, re.M)}
    items = lambda name: [s.strip() for s in re.split(r"\n(?=- )", sec.get(name, "")) if s.strip().startswith("- ")]
    label = lambda it: (re.match(r"- ([RI]\d+)", it) or re.match(r"- (.{0,30})", it)).group(1)
    fails = []
    if not sec.get("Outcome", "").strip():
        fails.append("the Outcome section is empty")
    reqs = items("Requirements")
    if not reqs and sid != "S00":  # S00 holds only the product's invariants
        fails.append("the spec states no requirement")
    for it in reqs:
        if not re.match(r"- R\d+: \S", it):
            fails.append(f"a requirement has no id: {it[:40]}")
        elif w := re.search(r"\b(fast|simple|intuitive|easy|user-friendly)\b", it, re.I):
            fails.append(f"{label(it)} says \"{w.group(1)}\": state it so that someone else can measure it")
    num = sid[1:]
    for it in items("Invariants"):  # the name, in any case, with spaces or underscores, as missing_tests matches it
        if not re.search(rf"Test: `s{num}[ _]{label(it)}\b", it, re.I):
            fails.append(f"{label(it)} names no test starting with `{sid} {label(it)}`")
    cited = {i for t in tasks() if get_line(t, "spec").split()[:1] == [sid] for i in re.findall(r"\bI\d+\b", get_line(t, "spec"))}
    for name in missing_tests(path, os.environ.get("MAIN", "main")):  # a test still to write is a task before the build
        inv = re.search(r"\bI\d+\b", name, re.I)
        if inv and inv.group(0).upper() not in cited:
            fails.append(f"no task writes the test of {inv.group(0).upper()}: xs file --priority p1 --spec \"{sid} {inv.group(0).upper()}\" \"...\", "
                         "and give the build tasks after: it")
    for it in [i for name in sec for i in items(name)] + [l for l in text.splitlines() if "[ASSUMPTION]" in l and not l.startswith("- ")]:
        if "[ASSUMPTION]" in it:
            fails.append(f"{label(it)} is an unconfirmed [ASSUMPTION]: ask the owner")
    for it in items("Open"):
        if not re.search(r"\b(task|spike|question)\b", it, re.I):
            fails.append(f"open item \"{it[2:40]}\" has no route: task, spike or question")
    for it in items("Decisions"):
        m = re.match(r"- ADR (\d{4})\b", it)
        if not m:
            fails.append(f"decision has no ADR: {it[2:40]}")
        elif not glob.glob(f"project/adr/{m.group(1)}-*.md"):
            fails.append(f"ADR {m.group(1)} does not exist in project/adr")
        elif status_of(f"ADR-{m.group(1)}") != "accepted":
            fails.append(f"ADR {m.group(1)} is not accepted: xs adr {m.group(1)} accepted, by the owner")
    owner = words(get_line(path, "owner"))
    waived = os.path.exists("AGENTS.md") and re.search(r"^- Spec approval:\s*none\b", open("AGENTS.md").read(), re.M | re.I)
    approvers = {e["kv"].get("by", "").lower() for e in events() if e["subj"] == sid and e["kind"] == "spec.approved"}
    if not owner:
        fails.append("the spec names no owner")
    elif owner.lower() not in approvers and not waived:
        fails.append(f"{owner} has not approved the spec: xs spec {sid} approved \"what\", run by {owner}")
    return fails


def cmd_adr(args):
    """An ADR's file is its decision, never edited; its status, Built and Amended by are events."""
    kinds = ("proposed", "accepted", "amended", "built", "retired")
    if len(args) not in (2, 3) or args[1] not in kinds or (args[1] in ("amended", "built") and len(args) == 2) \
            or (args[1] == "built" and not re.match(r"(no|partly|yes)\b", args[2])):
        die('usage: xs adr 0007 proposed|accepted|retired ["line"], xs adr 0007 built "no|partly|yes (T12)", '
            'or xs adr 0007 amended "ADR 0009 (what changed)"')
    num, kind = re.sub(r"^ADR-?", "", args[0]), args[1]
    if not re.match(r"\d{4}$", num) or len(glob.glob(f"project/adr/{num}-*.md")) != 1:
        die(f"{args[0]}: no single ADR file in project/adr")
    line = args[2].rstrip(".") if len(args) == 3 else ""
    sid = f"ADR-{num}"

    def prepare():
        status = kind if kind in ("proposed", "accepted", "retired") else status_of(sid, "proposed")
        extra = {"built": words(line)} if kind == "built" else {"amended": words(line)} if kind == "amended" else {"note": words(line) or None}
        return [ev(sid, f"adr.{kind}", status=status, **extra, by=actor())], [], f"xs: {sid} {kind}", status
    status = txn(prepare)
    print(f"{sid} {kind}: {status}")


# --- events with no file ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def record(line, msg):
    txn(lambda: ([line], [], msg, None))


def cmd_release(args):
    sha = opt(args, "--commit")
    if len(args) != 1:
        die("usage: xs release <name> [--commit <sha>]")
    record(ev(args[0], "released", commit=sha, by=actor()), f"xs: release {args[0]}")
    print(f"{args[0]} released")


def cmd_rollback(args):
    if len(args) != 2:
        die('usage: xs rollback <name> "reason"')
    record(ev(args[0], "rolled-back", reason=words(args[1]), by=actor()), f"xs: roll back {args[0]}")
    print(f"{args[0]} rolled back")


def cmd_incident(args):
    """An incident is open from incident.opened to incident.resolved: flow reads the time to restore."""
    sev = opt(args, "--sev", "2")
    if sev not in ("1", "2", "3", "4") or not ((len(args) == 3 and args[0] == "open") or (len(args) == 2 and args[0] == "resolve")):
        die('usage: xs incident open <slug> "line" [--sev 1|2|3|4], or xs incident resolve <slug>')
    slug = args[1]

    def prepare():
        kinds = [e["kind"] for e in events() if e["subj"] == slug and e["kind"] in ("incident.opened", "incident.resolved")]
        is_open = bool(kinds) and kinds[-1] == "incident.opened"
        if args[0] == "open" and is_open:
            die(f"incident {slug} is already open")
        if args[0] == "resolve" and not is_open:
            die(f"no open incident {slug} in the ledger")
        line = ev(slug, "incident.opened", what=words(args[2]), sev=sev, by=actor()) if args[0] == "open" else ev(slug, "incident.resolved", by=actor())
        return [line], [], f"xs: incident {slug} {args[0]}", None
    txn(prepare)
    print(f"incident {slug} {'opened' if args[0] == 'open' else 'resolved'}")


def cmd_void(args):
    """The log only grows: a wrong event is cancelled by a later one that names it. flow and xs skip both."""
    if len(args) != 4 or not re.match(r"\d{4}-\d\d-\d\dT\d\d:\d\d:\d\dZ$", args[2]):
        die('usage: xs void <subject> <kind> <at of the wrong event, as in the log> "reason"')
    subj, kind, at, reason = args

    def prepare():
        if not any(e["subj"] == subj and e["kind"] == kind and e["at"] == at for e in events()):
            die(f"no event {subj} {kind} at {at} in the ledger")
        return [ev(subj, "event.voided", of_kind=kind, of_at=at, reason=words(reason), by=actor())], [], f"xs: void {subj} {kind}", None
    txn(prepare)
    print(f"voided {subj} {kind} {at}")


# --- the view -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def cmd_status(args):
    """The ledger as text: what agents and people read instead of a status line in a file."""
    st = state()
    if args == ["--unlanded"]:
        for t, d in sorted(st.items()):
            if re.match(r"T\d+$", t) and d.get("status") == "closed":
                last = d["last"]
                why = f"ejected, {last['kv'].get('reason')}" if last["kind"] == "land.ejected" else "waiting for the integrator, or not delivered"
                print(f"{t} closed on {d.get('branch', '?')}: {why}")
        return
    if len(args) == 2 and args[0] == "--since":  # the report: what changed since the last one
        since = args[1] if "T" in args[1] else args[1] + "T00:00:00Z"
        for e in events():
            if e["at"] >= since:
                print(e["line"].replace(f" {scope()} ", " ", 1))
        return
    if len(args) == 1:
        i = args[0]
        files = glob.glob(lpath("tasks", f"{i}-*.md")) + glob.glob(lpath("learnings", f"{i}-*.md")) + \
            glob.glob(f"project/specs/{i}-*.md") + glob.glob(f"project/adr/{i.replace('ADR-', '')}-*.md" if i.startswith("ADR-") else "")
        d = st.get(i, {})
        print(f"{i}: {d.get('status') or (spec_status(i) if re.match(r'S\d+$', i) else 'no events')}"
              + "".join(f", {k} {d[k]}" for k in ("branch", "built", "amended") if d.get(k)) + "".join(f"\n  {f}" for f in files))
        for e in events():
            if e["subj"] == i:
                print("  " + e["line"])
        log = lpath("logs", f"{i}.md")
        if os.path.exists(log):
            print(f"Log ({log}):\n" + open(log).read().rstrip())
        return
    if args:
        die("usage: xs status [T12|S03|ADR-0007|L02] | --unlanded | --since <YYYY-MM-DD or time>")
    for p in tasks():
        t, d = ident(p), st.get(ident(p), {})
        if d.get("status") not in ("done", "dropped"):
            last = d.get("last", {})
            flag = f" (ejected: {last['kv'].get('reason')})" if last.get("kind") == "land.ejected" else ""
            print(f"{t} {d.get('status', '?')}{' on ' + d['branch'] if d.get('branch') and d.get('status') != 'todo' else ''}{flag} "
                  f"{get(p, 'priority')} {get_line(p, 'title')}")
            for run, e in sorted(d.get("agents", {}).items(), key=lambda r: r[1]["at"]):
                kv = e["kv"]
                if e["kind"] == "agent.started":
                    print(f"  agent {run} running since {e['at']}" + "".join(f", {kv[k]}" for k in ("role", "tool", "model", "effort") if kv.get(k)))
                elif e["kind"] == "agent.stopped":
                    print(f"  agent {run} stopped at {e['at']}: {kv.get('reason')}" + (f", resumes at {kv['resume_at']}" if kv.get("resume_at") else "")
                          + (f" (job {kv['job']})" if kv.get("job") else (", no resume scheduled" if kv.get("reason") == "limit" else "")))
    for f in sorted(glob.glob("project/specs/S*-*.md")):
        print(f"{ident(f)} {spec_status(ident(f))}")
    for f in sorted(glob.glob("project/adr/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-*.md")):
        d = st.get(f"ADR-{ident(f)}", {})
        print(f"ADR-{ident(f)} {d.get('status', 'no events')}" + "".join(f", {k} {d[k]}" for k in ("built", "amended") if d.get(k)))
    for p in entries("proposed") + entries("stale"):
        print(f"{ident(p)} {status_of(ident(p))} {get(p, 'kind')} to {get(p, 'to')}")


# --- memory -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DEST = {"rule": "AGENTS.md", "design": "DESIGN.md", "knowledge": "CONTEXT.md"}
ELSEWHERE = {"preference": "write it in your person's preferences: the only entry an agent writes directly",
             "decision": "a decision is the owner's: xs ask", "idea": "xs idea", "status": "status lives in a task: xs file"}


def learning(lid):
    hits = glob.glob(lpath("learnings", f"{lid}-*.md"))
    if len(hits) != 1:
        die(f"{lid}: no single entry in {lpath('learnings')}")
    return hits[0]


def text_of(path):
    _, m = front(path)
    return open(path).read()[m.end():].split("\n## ")[0].strip()


def cmd_idea(args):
    source = opt(args, "--source", "owner")
    if len(args) != 1:
        die('usage: xs idea [--source TEXT] "idea"')

    def prepare():
        with open(lpath("IDEAS.md"), "a") as f:
            f.write(f"- {dt.date.today().isoformat()} {args[0]} ({source})\n")
        return [ev("-", "idea.recorded", by=actor())], ["IDEAS.md"], "xs: idea", None
    txn(prepare)
    print(f"recorded in {lpath('IDEAS.md')}")


def cmd_propose(args):
    kind, anchor, evidence = opt(args, "--kind"), opt(args, "--anchor"), opt(args, "--evidence")
    to, sc, old = opt(args, "--to", DEST.get(kind, "")), opt(args, "--scope", ""), opt(args, "--replaces")
    if old and status_of(old) != "stale":
        die(f"{old} is {status_of(old) or 'unknown'}: --replaces takes a stale entry")
    if kind in ELSEWHERE:
        die(f"a {kind} is not proposed: {ELSEWHERE[kind]}")
    if kind not in DEST or not anchor or not evidence or len(args) != 1:
        die('usage: xs propose --kind rule|design|knowledge --anchor PATH --evidence TEXT [--to FILE] [--scope S] [--replaces L3] "entry"')
    slug = "-".join(re.findall(r"[a-z0-9]+", args[0].lower())[:6]) or "entry"

    def prepare():
        lid = next_id("learnings", "L")
        path = lpath("learnings", f"{lid}-{slug}.md")
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
        open(path, "w").write(f"---\nkind: {kind}\nto: {to}\nscope: {sc or scope()}\nanchor: {anchor}\n"
                              f"{'replaces: ' + old + chr(10) if old else ''}created: {dt.date.today().isoformat()}\n---\n\n{args[0]}\n\n## Evidence\n\n- {evidence}\n")
        line = ev(lid, "learning.proposed", status="proposed", type=kind, to=to, anchor=anchor, by=actor(), **({"replaces": old} if old else {}))
        return [line], [rel(path)], f"xs: propose {lid}", (lid, path)
    lid, path = txn(prepare)
    print(f"{lid} {path}: proposed to the owner of {to}")


def mark(path, lid, new):
    """Rewrite or remove the line marked (lid) in a destination file; return True if found."""
    if not os.path.exists(path):
        return False
    lines = open(path).read().split("\n")
    hit = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if re.search(rf"\({lid}[,)]", l)]
    for i in reversed(hit):
        if new is None:
            del lines[i]
        else:
            lines[i] = re.sub(rf"\({lid}[,)].*$", new, lines[i])
    open(path, "w").write("\n".join(lines))
    return bool(hit)


def write_dest(path, lid, text):
    if not os.path.exists(path):
        open(path, "w").write(f"# {os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(path))[0].title()}\n\n")
    lines = open(path).read().rstrip("\n").split("\n")
    nums = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if re.match(r"\d+\. ", l)]
    if nums:  # a numbered rules file: the next number, after the last rule
        n = int(re.match(r"(\d+)", lines[nums[-1]]).group(1)) + 1
        lines.insert(nums[-1] + 1, f"{n}. {text} ({lid})")
    else:
        lines.append(f"- {text} ({lid})")
    open(path, "w").write("\n".join(lines) + "\n")


def cmd_promote(args):
    if len(args) != 1:
        die("usage: xs promote L3")
    lid, path = args[0], learning(args[0])
    to = get(path, "to")

    def prepare():
        status = status_of(lid)
        if status not in ("proposed", "stale"):
            die(f"{lid} is {status}: only a proposed or stale entry is promoted")
        lines, files, old = [ev(lid, "learning.promoted", status="promoted", to=to, by=actor())], [rel(path)], get(path, "replaces")
        if old and status_of(old) not in ("checked", "retired"):  # the amended text takes the place of the stale entry
            op = learning(old)
            mark(get(op, "to"), old, None)
            with open(op, "a") as f:
                f.write(f"\nRetired: replaced by {lid}\n")
            lines.append(ev(old, "learning.retired", status="retired", by=actor(), replaced_by=lid))
            files.append(rel(op))
        return lines, files, f"xs: promote {lid}", status
    status = txn(prepare)
    if status == "proposed":  # on main, after the ledger: a retried prepare would write it twice
        write_dest(to, lid, text_of(path))
    else:
        mark(to, lid, f"({lid})")
    print(f"{lid} promoted: commit {to} on main")


def unload(args, kind, status, label):
    if len(args) != 2:
        die(f'usage: xs {sys.argv[1]} L3 "{label.lower()}"')
    lid, path = args[0], learning(args[0])

    def prepare():
        if status_of(lid) in ("checked", "retired"):
            die(f"{lid} is already {status_of(lid)}")
        mark(get(path, "to"), lid, None)
        with open(path, "a") as f:
            f.write(f"\n{label}: {args[1]}\n")
        return [ev(lid, kind, status=status, by=actor())], [rel(path)], f"xs: {status} {lid}", None
    txn(prepare)
    print(f"{lid} {status}: commit {get(path, 'to')} on main")


def cmd_recommend(args):
    if len(args) != 3 or args[1] not in ("holds", "retire"):
        die('usage: xs recommend L3 holds|retire "why"')
    lid, path = args[0], learning(args[0])

    def prepare():
        if status_of(lid) != "stale":
            die(f"{lid} is {status_of(lid)}: only a stale entry takes a recommendation")
        with open(path, "a") as f:
            f.write(f"\nRecommended ({dt.date.today().isoformat()}): {args[1]}, {args[2]}\n")
        return [ev(lid, "learning.recommended", rec=args[1], by=actor())], [rel(path)], f"xs: recommend {lid}", None
    txn(prepare)
    print(f"{lid}: recommended {args[1]}")


def cmd_repeated(args):
    if len(args) != 2:
        die('usage: xs repeated L3 "quote of the correction"')
    path = learning(args[0])

    def prepare():
        with open(path, "a") as f:
            f.write(f"- {dt.date.today().isoformat()}, repeated: {args[1]}\n")
        return [ev(args[0], "correction.repeated", by=actor())], [rel(path)], f"xs: {args[0]} repeated", None
    txn(prepare)
    print(f"{args[0]}: repeated")


def entries(status=None):
    return [p for p in sorted(glob.glob(lpath("learnings", "L*-*.md"))) if status is None or status_of(ident(p)) == status]


def cmd_queue(args):
    for p in tasks():
        if get(p, "type") == "decision" and status_of(ident(p)) in ("todo", "doing", "blocked"):
            print(f"{ident(p)} question {get_line(p, 'created')} {get_line(p, 'title')}")
    for p in entries("proposed") + entries("stale"):
        rec = re.findall(r"^Recommended \(.*?\): (.*)$", open(p).read(), re.M) if status_of(ident(p)) == "stale" else []
        extra = (f" (replaces {get(p, 'replaces')})" if get(p, "replaces") else "") + (f" [recommended: {rec[-1]}]" if rec else "")
        print(f"{ident(p)} {status_of(ident(p))} {get(p, 'kind')} to {get(p, 'to')}{extra}: {text_of(p)[:80]}")


def stale_marks(base, cwd):
    """Promoted entries whose anchor changed between base and HEAD in cwd: their line in the destination, under cwd,
    is marked stale. Returns the events to record once the change is on main."""
    changed = git("-C", cwd, "diff", "--name-only", f"{base}...HEAD").splitlines()
    lines, touched = [], set()
    for p in entries("promoted"):
        anchor = get(p, "anchor").rstrip("/")
        m = re.match(r"(S\d+|ADR-(\d{4}))$", anchor)
        prefix = (f"project/specs/{anchor}-" if m and not m.group(2) else f"project/adr/{m.group(2)}-") if m else None
        hit = next((c for c in changed if (c.startswith(prefix) if prefix else c == anchor or c.startswith(anchor + "/"))), None)
        if not hit:
            continue
        lid, to = ident(p), get(p, "to")
        mark(os.path.join(cwd, to), lid, f"({lid}, stale: {hit} changed)")
        touched.add(to)
        lines.append(ev(lid, "learning.stale", status="stale", anchor=hit, by="land"))
    return lines, sorted(touched)


def cmd_stale(args):
    """Entries whose anchor this branch changed: stale until a person confirms them (xs promote)."""
    if len(args) != 1:
        die("usage: xs stale MAIN")
    lines, touched = stale_marks(args[0], os.getcwd())
    if lines:
        txn(lambda: (lines, [], "xs: stale entries", None))
    for f in touched:
        print(f)


def person_log():
    d = os.environ.get("XS_HOME") or os.path.expanduser("~/.xs")
    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
    return os.path.join(d, "events.log")


def recalled(ids, via):
    with open(person_log(), "a") as f:
        for i in ids:
            f.write(f"{now()} {scope()} {i} learning.recalled via={via} session={os.environ.get('XS_SESSION', '-')} by={actor()}\n")


def cmd_load(args):
    ids = [ident(p) for p in entries("promoted")]
    recalled(ids, "load")
    print(f"loaded {len(ids)} entries")


def cmd_search(args):
    # ponytail: word overlap, no meaning; replace the scoring with a semantic index behind this same command
    if len(args) != 1:
        die('usage: xs search "words"')
    terms = {w for w in re.findall(r"\w{3,}", args[0].lower())}
    files = [f for g in ("project/specs/*.md", "project/adr/*.md", lpath("tasks", "T*.md"), lpath("learnings", "L*.md"),
                         lpath("logs", "*.md"), lpath("IDEAS.md"), "AGENTS.md", "DESIGN.md", "CONTEXT.md", "ARCHITECTURE.md")
             for f in glob.glob(g)]
    hits = []
    for f in files:
        body = open(f).read().lower()
        score = sum(body.count(w) for w in terms)
        if score:
            hits.append((score, f))
    hits.sort(key=lambda h: (-h[0], h[1]))
    learn = lpath("learnings")
    for score, f in hits[:10]:
        tag = f" [{status_of(ident(f))}]" if f.startswith(learn) else ""
        print(f"{score:3d} {f}{tag}")
    recalled([ident(f) for _, f in hits[:10] if f.startswith(learn)], "search")


DELETED = "\0deleted"


def cmd_import_git(args):
    """filed, closed, dropped and landed from history; ADRs proposed, accepted and retired. Run once, then never sync.
    An exit counts as much as a birth: a file removed (an ADR rejected or merged, a task deleted) or a task
    dropped closes its entry, or flow would report it waiting for ever."""
    dry = "--dry-run" in args
    if any(" src=git" in e["line"] for e in events()):
        die("already imported: the ledger holds src=git events")
    main, found, seen = os.environ.get("MAIN", "main"), [], {}

    def walk(*extra):
        # the diff --git header is there even for an empty file, unlike the ---/+++ lines. A rename git does not
        # detect (a new name and new content in one commit) reads as a deletion plus an addition: a deletion is an
        # exit only if no file with the same id exists once the commit is over
        def ident(p):
            m = re.search(r"/(T\d+|\d{4})-", p)
            return m.group(1) if m else p
        cur = at = None
        touched, gone = set(), []
        def flush():
            alive = {ident(p) for p in touched - set(gone)}
            for p in gone:
                if ident(p) not in alive:
                    yield at, p, DELETED
        for line in git("log", "--reverse", "-M", "--format=C %cI", "-p", "-U0", *extra, "--", "project/tasks", "project/adr").splitlines():
            if line.startswith("C "):
                yield from flush()
                at, touched, gone = utc(line[2:]), set(), []
            elif line.startswith("diff --git "):
                cur = re.match(r"diff --git a/\S+ b/(\S+)", line).group(1)
                touched.add(cur)
                yield at, cur, None
            elif line.startswith("deleted file mode") and cur:
                gone.append(cur)
                cur = None
            elif cur and line.startswith("+") and not line.startswith("+++"):
                yield at, cur, line[1:]
        yield from flush()

    for at, f, line in walk():
        m = re.match(r"project/tasks/(T\d+)-.*\.md$", f or "") or re.match(r"project/adr/(\d{4})-.*\.md$", f or "")
        if not m:
            continue
        subj = m.group(1) if f.startswith("project/tasks") else f"ADR-{m.group(1)}"
        task = f.startswith("project/tasks")
        if line == DELETED and (subj, "end") not in seen:
            seen[(subj, "end")] = 1
            found.append((at, subj, "task.dropped" if task else "adr.retired", ("status=dropped " if task else "") + "reason=removed"))
        elif line == DELETED:
            continue
        elif line is not None and task and re.match(r"status:\s*dropped\b", line) and (subj, "end") not in seen:
            seen[(subj, "end")] = 1
            found.append((at, subj, "task.dropped", "status=dropped"))
        elif line is None and (subj, "new") not in seen:
            seen[(subj, "new")] = 1
            kv = ""
            if task and os.path.exists(f):  # type and priority as the file states them now: git kept no history of intent
                fm = re.match(r"---\n(.*?\n)---", open(f).read(), re.S)
                kv = " ".join(f"{k}={v}" for k, v in re.findall(r"^(type|priority):[ \t]*([^\s#]+)", fm.group(1) if fm else "", re.M))
            found.append((at, subj, "task.filed" if task else "adr.proposed", ("status=todo " + kv).strip() if task else ""))
        elif line is not None and task and re.match(r"status:\s*(done|merged)\b", line) and (subj, "closed") not in seen:
            seen[(subj, "closed")] = 1
            found.append((at, subj, "task.closed", "status=done"))
        elif line is not None and not task and re.match(r"(status:\s*)?(proposed|accepted)\b", line, re.I) \
                and re.search(r"(^|[,;.]\s*|status:\s*)accepted\b", line, re.I) and (subj, "acc") not in seen:
            # only the header line, in any case: "Accepted on …", "Proposed on …, accepted by …"; never the body
            seen[(subj, "acc")] = 1
            found.append((at, subj, "adr.accepted", ""))
    for at, f, line in walk("--first-parent", "-m", main):
        m = re.match(r"project/tasks/(T\d+)-.*\.md$", f)
        if m and line is not None and re.match(r"status:\s*(done|merged)\b", line) and (m.group(1), "landed") not in seen:
            seen[(m.group(1), "landed")] = 1
            found.append((at, m.group(1), "landed", f"on={main}"))
    sc = scope()
    lines = [f"{at} {sc} {subj} {kind} {kv} src=git".replace("  ", " ") + "\n"
             for at, subj, kind, kv in sorted(found, key=lambda e: e[0])]  # stable: closed before landed
    if dry:
        sys.stdout.write("".join(lines))
        return
    txn(lambda: (lines, [], "xs: import the events git can date", None))
    print(f"imported {len(found)} events into the ledger; starts are not in git, so cycle time begins with xs start")


def cmd_integrate(args):
    """The integrator: the only process that moves main. Workers deliver with land and go on writing code.

    xs integrate                                   take every branch in the queue onto main, until it is empty
    xs integrate --deliver BRANCH WORKTREE KEEP    land's half: queue the branch, then wait for its outcome
    xs integrate --deliver ... --queue             queue it, start an integrator if none runs, return at once
    xs integrate --deliver ... --tip SHA           pin the commit to land (default: the branch's tip now)

    A round puts every queued branch, in order, on top of main in a worktree of its own. A branch that conflicts
    is ejected. CHECK_GATE (default: make check) runs once on the whole round. Green: main moves to it by
    fast-forward, a compare-and-swap that fails if main moved meanwhile, and the round is rebuilt (three times
    at most). Red: the first half is tried alone and the rest waits for the next round, down to the one branch
    that fails, which is ejected with its log. The queue entry pins the commit land saw: while the round is
    built, a branch whose ref no longer points to it (moved or deleted after land) is ejected as moved, and the
    round is rebuilt without it; a round picks the pinned commits, never what the ref holds later. After landing,
    a branch whose ref moved since is kept, with its worktree. An entry with no pin (queued before it) lands the
    ref as it is. The pin holds against an agent that can write refs, not one that can write the queue: the guard
    denies agents the queue and the lock. An ejected branch stays as it was; land.ejected records why.
    Queue, outcomes, logs and the lock live in the git dir, never in the repo."""
    common = git("rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir")
    qdir, lock = os.path.join(common, "xs-queue"), os.path.join(common, "xs-integrate.lock")
    done, logs = os.path.join(qdir, "done"), os.path.join(qdir, "logs")
    os.makedirs(done, exist_ok=True)
    os.makedirs(logs, exist_ok=True)
    main = os.environ.get("MAIN", "main")
    gate = os.environ.get("CHECK_GATE") or os.environ.get("CHECK") or "make check"
    main_wt = re.match(r"worktree (.+)", git("worktree", "list", "--porcelain")).group(1)
    tw = os.path.join(main_wt, ".xs", "worktrees", "_integrate")
    if git("-C", main_wt, "branch", "--show-current") != main:
        die(f"{main_wt} is not on {main}: the integrator moves {main} there, and leaves it alone")
    say = lambda m: print(f"land: {m}", flush=True)

    def log_events(lines, msg):
        """A ledger that cannot be written must not stop the round once main moved, or the branch would land twice
        and land would wait for ever: the events wait in the git dir, and the next xs command writes them."""
        try:
            txn(lambda: (lines, [], msg, None))
        except SystemExit as e:
            subprocess.run(["git", "-C", ledger(), "checkout", "HEAD", "--", LOG], capture_output=True)
            open(unrecorded(), "a").writelines(lines)
            say(f"the ledger refused the events ({e}); the next xs command writes them")

    def acquire():
        try:
            os.mkdir(lock)
        except FileExistsError:
            try:
                pid = int(open(os.path.join(lock, "pid")).read())
                os.kill(pid, 0)
                return False
            except (OSError, ValueError):  # the holder died: take the lock over
                subprocess.run(["rm", "-rf", lock])
                return acquire()
        open(os.path.join(lock, "pid"), "w").write(str(os.getpid()))
        return True

    def queued():
        out = []
        for name in sorted(os.listdir(qdir)):
            p = os.path.join(qdir, name)
            if re.match(r"\d+-", name) and os.path.isfile(p):
                branch, wt, keep, tip = (open(p).read().split("\n") + [""])[:4]  # an entry from before the pin has no tip
                out.append(dict(file=p, branch=branch, wt=wt, keep=keep == "keep", tip=tip))
        return out

    def run(*a, cwd=tw):
        return subprocess.run(["git", "-C", cwd, *a], capture_output=True, text=True)

    def outcome(e, text):
        open(os.path.join(done, e["branch"]), "w").write(text)
        os.remove(e["file"])

    def tasks_closed(branch):
        """The tasks closed on this branch and not yet landed: their state is in the ledger, never in the branch."""
        global _state
        _state = None
        return sorted((t for t, d in state().items() if re.match(r"T\d+$", t) and d.get("status") == "closed" and d.get("branch") == branch),
                      key=lambda t: int(t[1:])) or ["-"]

    def reset():
        if not os.path.isdir(tw):
            git("worktree", "add", "-q", "--detach", tw, main)
        run("reset", "-q", "--hard", main)
        run("clean", "-qfd")  # untracked build caches in ignored folders stay: the next round compiles less

    def eject(e, reason, detail):
        lines = [ev(t, "land.ejected", branch=e["branch"], reason=reason, by="land") for t in tasks_closed(e["branch"])]
        log_events(lines, f"land: eject {e['branch']} ({reason})")
        outcome(e, f"ejected {reason}\n{detail}\n")
        say(f"ejected {e['branch']}: {reason}. {detail}")

    def round_(entries):
        reset()
        base, picked = run("rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip(), []
        for e in entries:
            if e["tip"]:  # the ref was written after land: what it points to now was never checked nor reviewed
                now = run("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"refs/heads/{e['branch']}^{{commit}}").stdout.strip()
                if now != e["tip"]:
                    eject(e, "moved", f"{e['branch']} is at {now or 'nothing'}, not at {e['tip']} as delivered by land: "
                                      f"reset it to what was delivered (git branch -f {e['branch']} {e['tip']}) "
                                      f"or review what changed, then land it again")
                    return True
            before = run("rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip()
            # the pinned tip, not the ref: a write between this check and the pick lands nothing it did not see
            commits = git("rev-list", "--reverse", "--no-merges", f"{main}..{e['tip'] or e['branch']}").split()
            r = run("cherry-pick", "--allow-empty", "--keep-redundant-commits", *commits) if commits else None
            if r is not None and r.returncode:
                files = run("diff", "--name-only", "--diff-filter=U").stdout.split() or ["see git rebase " + main]  # before the abort clears them
                run("cherry-pick", "--abort")
                run("reset", "-q", "--hard", before)
                eject(e, "conflict", f"rebase {e['branch']} on {main} and resolve: {' '.join(files)}")
                return True
            picked.append(e)
        if not picked:
            return True
        logf = os.path.join(logs, f"gate-{time_ns()}.log")
        say(f"{gate}, on {' '.join(e['branch'] for e in picked)}")
        green = subprocess.run(["bash", "-c", gate], cwd=tw, stdout=open(logf, "w"), stderr=subprocess.STDOUT).returncode == 0
        if not green:
            if len(picked) == 1:
                eject(picked[0], "red", f"the gate failed: {logf}")
                return True
            return round_(picked[:len(picked) // 2])  # the rest waits for the next round
        stale, touched = stale_marks(base, tw)  # memory entries whose anchor the round changed: their mark is content, on main
        if touched:
            run("add", "--", *touched)
            run("commit", "-q", "-m", "land: mark stale entries", "--", *touched)
        r = run("merge", "--ff-only", "-q", run("rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip(), cwd=main_wt)
        if r.returncode:
            return False  # main moved under the round: rebuild it
        head = git("rev-parse", "--short", main)
        lines = [ev(t, "landed", status="done" if t != "-" else None, on=main, commit=head, branch=e["branch"], by="land")
                 for e in picked for t in tasks_closed(e["branch"])]
        log_events(lines + stale, "land: " + " ".join(e["branch"] for e in picked))  # main has moved: never stop here
        for e in picked:
            note = ""
            now = run("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"refs/heads/{e['branch']}^{{commit}}").stdout.strip()
            if e["tip"] and now != e["tip"]:  # written during the round: what it holds now did not land, keep it
                note = f"; kept {e['branch']} and its worktree: its ref moved to {now or 'nothing'} after land"
            elif e["keep"]:  # the chain goes on from what landed, or its next delivery would repeat these commits
                if not run("status", "--porcelain", cwd=e["wt"]).stdout:
                    run("reset", "-q", "--hard", main, cwd=e["wt"])
            elif os.path.isdir(e["wt"]) and run("worktree", "remove", e["wt"], cwd=main_wt).returncode == 0:
                run("branch", "-D", "-q", e["branch"], cwd=main_wt)
                note = f"; removed {e['wt']} and {e['branch']}"
            outcome(e, f"landed {head}{note}\n")
            say(f"{main} is now {head}, {e['branch']} landed{note}")
        return True

    if "--deliver" in args:
        i = args.index("--deliver")
        branch, wt, keep = args[i + 1:i + 4]
        tip = git("rev-parse", "--verify", (args[args.index("--tip") + 1] if "--tip" in args else f"refs/heads/{branch}") + "^{commit}")
        open(os.path.join(qdir, f"{time_ns()}-{branch.replace('/', '_')}"), "w").write(f"{branch}\n{wt}\n{keep}\n{tip}\n")
        result = os.path.join(done, branch)
        if os.path.exists(result):
            os.remove(result)
        if "--queue" in args:
            if not os.path.exists(lock):
                subprocess.Popen([os.path.abspath(__file__), "integrate"], cwd=main_wt, start_new_session=True,
                                 stdout=open(os.path.join(logs, "integrate.log"), "a"), stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
            say(f"{branch} queued: the integrator lands it; its outcome goes to the log and to {result}")
            return
        while not os.path.exists(result):  # wait: integrate if no one does, or let the integrator work
            if acquire():
                try:
                    integrate_all(queued, round_, say)
                finally:
                    subprocess.run(["rm", "-rf", lock])
            else:
                import time
                time.sleep(1)
        text = open(result).read()
        if not text.startswith("landed"):
            print(text.strip(), file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(1)
        return
    while acquire():  # after the lock is released, a branch queued meanwhile would wait for ever: look again
        try:
            integrate_all(queued, round_, say)
        finally:
            subprocess.run(["rm", "-rf", lock])
        if not queued():
            break


def integrate_all(queued, round_, say):
    misses = 0
    while queued():
        if round_(queued()):
            misses = 0
        else:
            misses += 1
            if misses == 3:
                die("main kept moving under the round, or its worktree has changes the fast-forward would overwrite")


def time_ns():
    import time
    return time.time_ns()


ADR_STATE = re.compile(r"^(Proposed|Accepted|Retired|Rejected|Superseded)\b|^(Built|Amended by):")


def cmd_migrate(args):
    """Once, in a repo that kept its tracker on main: move EVENTS.log, tasks, learnings and IDEAS.md to the ledger
    without their state lines, move each spec's Log to logs/, remove the state lines of specs and ADRs, and record a
    migrated event wherever a file's state differed from its events. The changes on main are left to commit."""
    main = os.environ.get("MAIN", "main")
    if args or git("branch", "--show-current") != main or os.path.realpath(os.getcwd()) != os.path.realpath(main_wt()):
        die(f"usage: xs migrate, on {main} in the main worktree")
    old = [p for p in ("project/EVENTS.log", "project/tasks", "project/learnings", "project/IDEAS.md") if os.path.exists(p)]
    if not old and not glob.glob("project/specs/S*-*.md") and not glob.glob("project/adr/[0-9]*-*.md"):
        die("nothing to migrate: project/ holds no EVENTS.log, tasks, learnings, IDEAS.md, specs or ADRs")
    onmain = {}  # the rewritten specs and ADRs: written after the ledger's commit, since a retry runs prepare again
    old_text = open("project/EVENTS.log").read() if os.path.exists("project/EVENTS.log") else ""
    before = state_of(events(old_text))
    has = lambda i: before.get(i, {}).get("status", "")
    VOCAB = {"task": ("todo", "doing", "blocked", "closed", "done", "dropped"),
             "learning": ("proposed", "promoted", "stale", "checked", "retired")}

    def strip_state(text, keys):
        m = re.match(r"---\n(.*?\n)---\n", text, re.S)
        if not m:
            return text, {}
        found = dict(re.findall(rf"^({'|'.join(keys)}):[ \t]*([^\s#]*)", m.group(1), re.M))
        fm = re.sub(rf"^({'|'.join(keys)}):.*\n", "", m.group(1), flags=re.M)
        return "---\n" + fm + "---\n" + text[m.end():], found

    def prepare():
        if events():  # after the pull: a teammate may have migrated already
            die("the ledger already holds events: migrate runs once")
        onmain.clear()
        extra, paths, n = [], [], {"tasks": 0, "learnings": 0, "specs": 0, "adrs": 0, "migrated": 0}
        for kind, folder, prefix in (("task", "tasks", "T"), ("learning", "learnings", "L")):
            for f in sorted(glob.glob(f"project/{folder}/*")):
                name = os.path.basename(f)
                dst = lpath(folder, name)
                if name == "RESERVED":
                    continue  # one ledger hands out the numbers: no ranges
                if os.path.isdir(f):  # an archive, kept as it was
                    shutil.copytree(f, dst, dirs_exist_ok=True)
                    paths.append(rel(dst))
                    continue
                os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
                if not re.match(rf"{prefix}\d+-.*\.md$", name):
                    shutil.copy(f, dst)  # a README or a saved patch
                    paths.append(rel(dst))
                    continue
                text, found = strip_state(open(f).read(), ("status", "branch", "closed", "blocked_reason"))
                open(dst, "w").write(text)
                paths.append(rel(dst))
                n[folder] += 1
                i, st = ident(f), found.get("status", "")
                st = "done" if kind == "task" and st in ("merged", "closed") else st  # on main: it landed
                was = None
                if st not in VOCAB[kind] and not has(i):  # missing or outside the vocabulary: it starts over, the old word kept
                    st, was = ("todo" if kind == "task" else "proposed"), (words(st) or "none")
                if st in VOCAB[kind] and st != has(i):
                    extra.append(ev(i, f"{kind}.migrated", status=st, branch=found.get("branch") or None, was=was, src="migrate"))
        if os.path.exists("project/IDEAS.md"):
            shutil.copy("project/IDEAS.md", lpath("IDEAS.md"))
            paths.append("IDEAS.md")
        for f in sorted(glob.glob("project/specs/S*-*.md")):
            text, found = strip_state(open(f).read(), ("status",))
            sid = ident(f)
            m = re.search(r"^## Log[ \t]*\n(.*?)(?=^## |\Z)", text, re.M | re.S)
            if m:
                log = [l for l in m.group(1).splitlines() if l.strip()]
                text = (text[:m.start()].rstrip("\n") + "\n" + ("\n" + text[m.end():] if text[m.end():].strip() else "")).rstrip("\n") + "\n"
                if log:
                    dst = lpath("logs", f"{sid}.md")
                    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
                    open(dst, "w").write("\n".join(log) + "\n")
                    paths.append(rel(dst))
                approved = {e["kv"].get("by", "").lower() for e in events(old_text) if e["subj"] == sid and e["kind"] == "spec.approved"}
                for who in re.findall(r"approved by ([^\s:,.]+):", "\n".join(log), re.I):  # the form xs writes; "approved by that direction" is prose
                    if who.lower() not in approved:
                        approved.add(who.lower())
                        extra.append(ev(sid, "spec.approved", by=who, src="migrate"))
            onmain[f] = text
            n["specs"] += 1
            st = found.get("status", "")
            if st in ("draft", "ready", "done", "dropped") and st != (has(sid) or "draft"):
                extra.append(ev(sid, "spec.migrated", status=st, src="migrate"))
        for f in sorted(glob.glob("project/adr/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-*.md")):
            lines = open(f).read().split("\n")
            end = next((i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith("## ")), len(lines))
            head = [l for l in lines[1:end] if ADR_STATE.match(l)]
            if not head:
                continue
            sid, st, built, amended = f"ADR-{ident(f)}", "", "", ""
            for l in head:
                k = ADR_STATE.match(l)
                if k.group(1):
                    st = k.group(1).lower()
                elif k.group(2) == "Built":
                    built = words(l.split(":", 1)[1])
                else:
                    amended = words(l.split(":", 1)[1])
            keep = lines[:1] + [l for l in lines[1:end] if not ADR_STATE.match(l)] + lines[end:]
            onmain[f] = re.sub(r"\n{3,}", "\n\n", "\n".join(keep))
            n["adrs"] += 1
            d = before.get(sid, {})
            if (st and st != d.get("status")) or (built and built != d.get("built")) or (amended and amended != d.get("amended")):
                extra.append(ev(sid, "adr.migrated", status=st or None, built=built or None, amended=amended or None, src="migrate"))
        n["migrated"] = len(extra)
        lines = [l if l.endswith("\n") else l + "\n" for l in old_text.splitlines(keepends=True)] + extra
        return lines, paths, "xs: migrate the ledger from main", n
    n = txn(prepare)
    for f, text in onmain.items():
        open(f, "w").write(text)
    if old:
        git("rm", "-r", "-q", "--", *old)
    if os.path.exists(".gitattributes"):
        keep = [l for l in open(".gitattributes").read().splitlines() if not re.match(r"project/(EVENTS\.log|tasks/RESERVED)\s", l)]
        open(".gitattributes", "w").write("".join(l + "\n" for l in keep))
    print(f"moved {n['tasks']} tasks and {n['learnings']} entries to {ledger()} (branch {LEDGER}); "
          f"moved the Log of {n['specs']} specs; removed the state lines of {n['adrs']} ADRs; {n['migrated']} migrated events.\n"
          f"Review the diff on {main}, then commit it: git commit -am \"Move the ledger off main\"")



def tools(home):
    """The adapters whose tool is installed in HOME. ponytail: one adapter today; a manifest per adapter when a second one needs files."""
    return [t for t, d in [("claude-code", ".claude")] if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(home, d))]


def cmd_install(args, here):
    """Link the skills into the agent tools found in HOME, and apply each tool's adapter. Run again, it changes nothing."""
    xs, home = os.path.dirname(here), os.path.expanduser("~")
    dirs = [d for d in [opt(args, "--skills-dir")] if d]
    claude = os.path.join(home, ".claude") if "claude-code" in tools(home) else None
    if claude:
        dirs.append(os.path.join(claude, "skills"))
    if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(home, ".agents")) or os.path.isdir(os.path.join(home, ".codex")):
        dirs.append(os.path.join(home, ".agents", "skills"))  # the tools that read the open standard from ~/.agents
    if not dirs:
        die("no agent tool found in ~: pass --skills-dir <your tool's skills folder>")
    adapter = os.path.join(xs, "adapters", "claude-code")
    links = [(os.path.join(xs, "skills", n), os.path.join(d, n)) for d in dirs
             for n in sorted(os.listdir(os.path.join(xs, "skills"))) if os.path.exists(os.path.join(xs, "skills", n, "SKILL.md"))]
    if claude:  # the role definitions of the adapter
        links += [(os.path.join(adapter, "agents", n), os.path.join(claude, "agents", n))
                  for n in sorted(os.listdir(os.path.join(adapter, "agents"))) if n.endswith(".md")]
    for src, dst in links:
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
        if os.path.realpath(dst) == os.path.realpath(src):
            continue
        if os.path.lexists(dst):
            print(f"kept {dst}: it exists and is not XS's; remove it and run xs install again to link it")
            continue
        os.symlink(src, dst)
        print(f"linked {dst}")
    ours = (os.path.join(xs, "skills") + os.sep, os.path.join(adapter, "agents") + os.sep)
    for d in set(os.path.dirname(dst) for _, dst in links):  # a link of ours left by a renamed or removed skill
        for n in os.listdir(d):
            p = os.path.join(d, n)
            if os.path.islink(p) and not os.path.exists(p) and os.readlink(p).startswith(ours):
                os.remove(p)
                print(f"removed {p}: its target is gone")
    if claude:  # the adapter's hooks: the guard, and the lifecycle of subagents (xs agent events)
        path = os.path.join(claude, "settings.json")
        conf = json.load(open(path)) if os.path.exists(path) else {}
        hooks, changed = conf.setdefault("hooks", {}), False
        for event, matcher, name in [("PreToolUse", "Bash|Agent|Task", "guard"), ("PreToolUse", "Agent|Task", "lifecycle"),
                                     ("SubagentStop", None, "lifecycle")]:
            have = hooks.setdefault(event, [])
            ours = [m for m in have if any(h.get("command", "").endswith("/" + name) for h in m.get("hooks", []))]
            if not ours:
                have.append({**({"matcher": matcher} if matcher else {}),
                             "hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": f"python3 {os.path.join(adapter, name)}"}]})
                print(f"hook {name} on {event} added to {path}")
            for m in ours:  # an older install guarded Bash only
                if matcher and m.get("matcher") != matcher:
                    m["matcher"], changed = matcher, True
            changed = changed or not ours
        if changed:
            json.dump(conf, open(path, "w"), indent=2)
    if here not in os.environ.get("PATH", "").split(os.pathsep):
        print(f'add the scripts to PATH: export PATH="{here}:$PATH"')


def cmd_init(args, here):
    """Copy the template into the repo; a file already there is kept, and the two git files get only their missing lines."""
    xs, made, kept = os.path.dirname(here), [], []
    sources = [os.path.join(xs, "template")] + [os.path.join(xs, "adapters", t, "template") for t in tools(os.path.expanduser("~"))]
    for template, d, names in [(t, d, n) for t in sources for d, _, n in os.walk(t)]:
        if os.path.relpath(d, template).split(os.sep)[0] == "ledger":
            continue  # the ledger's files go to the ledger, which xs creates below
        for n in names:
            if n == ".DS_Store":
                continue
            src = os.path.join(d, n)
            dst = os.path.relpath(src, template)
            if n == ".gitattributes" and os.path.exists(dst):
                have = open(dst).read().splitlines()
                add = [l for l in open(src).read().splitlines() if l and not l.startswith("#") and l not in have]
                if add:
                    open(dst, "a").write("".join(l + "\n" for l in add))
                    made.append(dst + " (lines added)")
                continue
            if os.path.exists(dst):
                kept.append(dst)
                continue
            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst) or ".", exist_ok=True)
            shutil.copy(src, dst)
            made.append(dst)
    ignore = open(".gitignore").read().splitlines() if os.path.exists(".gitignore") else []
    if ".xs/" not in ignore:
        open(".gitignore", "a").write(".xs/\n")
        made.append(".gitignore (.xs/ ignored: the worktrees and the ledger's checkout)")
    made.append(f"{ledger()} (the ledger, branch {LEDGER})")
    for f in made:
        print(f"added {f}")
    for f in kept:
        print(f"kept {f}: compare it with XS's in {os.path.join(xs, 'template')} or its adapter")
    first = ("merge XS's rules into your AGENTS.md (the template is beside xs)" if "AGENTS.md" in kept
             else "fill each <...> of AGENTS.md: the stack, the commit rules")
    print(f"""
next:
  1. {first}; and give make the targets
     check-change, check and check-release (or set CHECK_CHANGE, CHECK_GATE, CHECK_RELEASE)
  2. git add what it added, and commit: "Adopt XS"
  3. ask your agent for a small change, ending with: "Use the lead skill."
""")


def main(argv):
    if not argv or argv[0] in ("-h", "--help"):
        print(__doc__.strip())
        return
    here = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))  # before the chdir: __file__ may be relative
    if argv[0] == "install":  # outside any repo
        return cmd_install(argv[1:], here)
    if argv[0] == "init" and subprocess.run(["git", "rev-parse"], capture_output=True).returncode:
        die("not a git repo: run git init first")
    os.chdir(git("rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"))
    cmd, args = argv[0], argv[1:]
    {"init": lambda a: cmd_init(a, here),
     "migrate": cmd_migrate,
     "status": cmd_status,
     "file": lambda a: file_task(a, "task.filed"),
     "ask": lambda a: file_task(a, "question.asked"),
     "next": cmd_next,
     "start": cmd_start,
     "agent": cmd_agent,
     "sync": cmd_sync,
     "handoff": cmd_handoff,
     "takeover": cmd_takeover,
     "close": lambda a: transition(a, "task.closed", "closed"),
     "answer": cmd_answer,
     "block": lambda a: transition(a, "task.blocked", "blocked", need_reason=True),
     "unblock": lambda a: transition(a, "task.unblocked", ""),
     "drop": lambda a: transition(a, "task.dropped", "dropped", need_reason=True),
     "spec": cmd_spec,
     "review": cmd_review,
     "reviewed": cmd_reviewed,
     "import-git": cmd_import_git,
     "void": cmd_void,
     "integrate": cmd_integrate,
     "where": lambda a: os.execv(os.path.join(here, "where"), [os.path.join(here, "where"), *a]),
     "land": lambda a: os.execv(os.path.join(here, "land"), [os.path.join(here, "land"), *a]),
     "idea": cmd_idea,
     "propose": cmd_propose,
     "promote": cmd_promote,
     "checked": lambda a: unload(a, "learning.checked", "checked", "Checked by"),
     "retire": lambda a: unload(a, "learning.retired", "retired", "Retired"),
     "repeated": cmd_repeated,
     "recommend": cmd_recommend,
     "queue": cmd_queue,
     "stale": cmd_stale,
     "load": cmd_load,
     "search": cmd_search,
     "adr": cmd_adr,
     "release": cmd_release,
     "rollback": cmd_rollback,
     "incident": cmd_incident,
     }.get(cmd, lambda a: die(f"unknown command {cmd}: xs --help"))(args)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main(sys.argv[1:])
